# Complete Vercel Deployment Guide (100% Vercel — Render Completely Removed)

This guide walks you through deploying both the **Backend** and **Frontend** on **Vercel**, especially if your previous Vercel account was deleted and you are setting it up fresh with your active Vercel account.

---

## 1. Handling the Deleted Vercel Account

If your previous Vercel account was deleted:
1. **Unlink / Clear any old local links**:
   - Any previous `.vercel` folders have been added to `.gitignore` and deleted.
   - If you use the Vercel CLI locally in terminal, log out and log in to your new account:
     ```bash
     npx vercel logout
     npx vercel login
     ```
2. **Push your code to GitHub**:
   - Commit all the latest changes and push them to your GitHub repository:
     ```bash
     git add .
     git commit -m "Configure full Vercel deployment and remove Render"
     git push origin main
     ```
3. **Log in to your new Vercel Account**:
   - Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) and log in with your current account.
   - Ensure your GitHub account is connected to Vercel.

